s": ["All ten expert raters place the seat at Safe or Solid D, and prediction markets price Bynum near 97 percent", "Bynum holds an overwhelming financial edge: $3.8 million raised and $2.7 million on hand versus $424,000 raised for Adair, with no outside spending against her", "The district's four-point Democratic lean combined with the 2026 environment and incumbency points to a wide margin", "No general-election polling exists, so the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings and markets, which all align"], "rationale": "Every available signal points the same direction: raters unanimously call the seat Safe or Solid Democratic, markets price Bynum around 96-97 percent, and she holds roughly a nine-to-one fundraising advantage with no outside opposition. With no polls to contradict the fundamentals, there is no evidence justifying a move away from the expected double-digit margin.", "watch": "A late-breaking scandal or a sharply shifted national environment could tighten the race, but nothing in current coverage, ratings or markets suggests movement toward Adair.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Janelle Bynum (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Janelle Bynum, the Democratic incumbent, is strongly favored to hold Oregon's 5th Congressional District against Republican Patti Adair. Every major forecaster rates the seat Safe or Solid for Democrats, and prediction markets price her chances near 97 percent. The district carries a four-point Democratic lean, and the 2026 environment adds to that advantage. With no general-election polling available, the outlook rests on fundamentals, ratings and markets, which all point the same way.\n\nMoney underscores the gap: Bynum has raised about $3.8 million and holds $2.7 million on hand, while Adair raised roughly $424,000 with $135,000 remaining, and no outside groups have spent against the incumbent. Local coverage has been favorable, including a September forecaster upgrade and the launch of Bynum's first TV ad. Running well-funded with a record of delivering federal projects for the district, Bynum enters November as the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9797, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.3}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9806, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9736, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9805, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9822, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9817, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9824, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.982, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9821, "margin": 15.5}]}